From: A9 project <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0059] drm/msm/dpu: observe video flush completion without an IRQ wakeup

A9's frame-progress latch cuts HV after three 85 Hz periods (~35.3 ms).
The saved AOD failure has zero ring underruns and a 53.97 ms DPU flush-wait
maximum. A waitqueue-only observation can hide an already-cleared CTL flush
register until the full 50 ms timeout when its IRQ wakeup is missing/delayed.
The original triggering event is not retained, so that mechanism is a
candidate cause of this capture rather than a proven hardware diagnosis.

Poll the identical register-zero completion predicate sleepably at up to
1 ms intervals, retaining the existing 50 ms DPU timeout. This changes
observation latency only: no nonzero flush is accepted; all A9 progress,
neutral, rail and abort interlocks remain unchanged. An actual stuck flush
still trips the independent A9 deadline and cannot silently recover.

Co-Authored-By: GPT-6.1 Sol <noreply@openai.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@
 #include "dpu_trace.h"
 #include "disp/msm_disp_snapshot.h"
 #include "msm_dsc_helper.h"
+
+#include <linux/iopoll.h>
 
 #include <drm/display/drm_dsc_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_managed.h>
@@ -538,17 +540,25 @@
 		struct dpu_encoder_phys *phys_enc)
 {
 	struct dpu_hw_ctl *hw_ctl = phys_enc->hw_ctl;
+	u32 flush;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!hw_ctl)
 		return 0;
 
-	ret = wait_event_timeout(phys_enc->pending_kickoff_wq,
-		(hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl) == 0),
-		msecs_to_jiffies(50));
-	if (ret <= 0) {
-		DPU_ERROR("vblank timeout: %x\n", hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register(hw_ctl));
-		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+	/*
+	 * A video-mode flush can complete even when the vsync wakeup is late
+	 * or lost. A single wait_event_timeout then hides completed hardware
+	 * progress until its entire 50 ms timeout, exceeding A9's independent
+	 * three-frame drive deadline. Observe the SAME completion predicate
+	 * directly, with sleepable 1 ms polling and the same 50 ms timeout.
+	 * No pending flush is accepted, and the A9 hardirq interlock is unchanged.
+	 */
+	ret = read_poll_timeout(hw_ctl->ops.get_flush_register, flush, !flush,
+				1000, 50000, false, hw_ctl);
+	if (ret) {
+		DPU_ERROR("vblank timeout: %x\n", flush);
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
